// Contamination canary: two calls returning DIFFERENT arrays, each asserted
// independently. Before the fix both calls came back holding the second call's
// data — the first call's element 0 read as 100 rather than 10 — because they
// shared one dead frame. A single-call fixture cannot see that.
fnc: [3: t64] mk(a: t64) { [a, a + 1, a + 2] }
p: [3: t64] = mk(10)
q: [3: t64] = mk(100)
print(p:[0])
print(p:[1])
print(p:[2])
print(q:[0])
print(q:[1])
print(q:[2])
